      "title": "0.1 Teaching contract",
      "number": "0.1",
      "line_start": 15,
      "line_end": 31,
      "kind": "curriculum_or_design_reference",
      "body": "For every concept or lesson, the teacher should be able to provide:\n\n1. **Plain-language meaning:** what the concept means without jargon.\n2. **Formal definition:** a precise, discipline-appropriate definition.\n3. **Mechanism:** how and why it occurs; distinguish cause, condition, trigger and consequence.\n4. **Spatial expression:** where it occurs, how it is distributed, at what scale, and why the pattern varies.\n5. **Temporal expression:** how it changes over minutes, seasons, geological time, decades or centuries.\n6. **Evidence:** observations, measurements, maps, data, field evidence, models or authoritative sources that support the explanation.\n7. **Boundary conditions:** where the rule works, where it fails, and what exceptions matter.\n8. **Misconceptions:** common plausible errors and how to diagnose them.\n9. **Representation:** a diagram, map, cross-section, graph, timeline, flow chart, field sketch or worked numerical example when useful.\n10. **Retrieval and transfer:** a short recall check and a new-context problem that tests understanding rather than wording.\n11. **Curriculum level:** the depth appropriate to the learner's class, followed by optional higher-level extensions.\n12. **Source and freshness:** NCERT class/book/chapter anchor, plus an authoritative current source when facts are time-sensitive.",
