      "title": "0.2 Source hierarchy and truth discipline",
      "number": "0.2",
      "line_start": 32,
      "line_end": 44,
      "kind": "curriculum_or_design_reference",
      "body": "Use the following hierarchy for different kinds of claims:\n\n- **Curriculum scope:** the relevant NCERT edition and current official examination syllabus.\n- **Stable scientific mechanism:** established physical geography, geomorphology, climatology, ecology, demography and spatial-science principles.\n- **Current facts:** current official statistical publications, government agencies, scientific observatories, international statistical agencies and dated datasets.\n- **Contested interpretation:** identify competing explanations, evidence and uncertainty rather than manufacturing consensus.\n- **Maps and boundaries:** use the latest appropriate official map source; do not blindly repeat old textbook map caveats or outdated administrative labels.\n- **UPSC relevance:** connect concepts to the official syllabus and previous-year question patterns only after checking those sources. Do not label a topic “frequently asked” without evidence.\n\nNever silently merge a textbook statement from an older edition with a current statistic. Store the source date and edition. When the teacher is uncertain, it should say what is uncertain and what would resolve it.",
