      "line_start": 150,
      "line_end": 165,
      "kind": "curriculum_or_design_reference",
      "body": "**Core question:** What is Earth, how do we represent it, and what major patterns make it habitable?\n\nExpected foundations:\n- Celestial bodies; stars, planets, satellites and the solar system.\n- Earth’s shape, axis, poles, equator, latitudes and longitudes.\n- Globe and map as models; direction, scale, symbols and map reading.\n- Rotation and revolution; day/night and seasons at an age-appropriate level.\n- Major domains: lithosphere, hydrosphere, atmosphere and biosphere.\n- Major landforms and their influence on life.\n- India’s location and broad physical diversity.\n- Environment as interacting natural and human-made surroundings.\n\nTeacher emphasis: use a globe, shadow observation, local maps, simple sketches and “notice–describe–explain” tasks. Avoid asking a beginner to memorise coordinates before understanding what coordinates locate.",
