      "body": "**Core question:** How do Earth's systems change, and how do people adapt to different environments?\n\nExpected foundations:\n- Natural, human-made and human components of environment.\n- Interior of Earth; crust, mantle and core; rocks and rock cycle.\n- Endogenic and exogenic processes; weathering, erosion, deposition and landform change.\n- Atmosphere, composition, temperature, pressure, winds and moisture.\n- Water cycle, ocean movements and water as a life-support system.\n- Natural vegetation and wildlife as climate–soil–water–organism relationships.\n- Settlement, transport and communication.\n- Human–environment interactions in tropical/subtropical regions, temperate grasslands and deserts.\n\nTeacher emphasis: make every regional example a causal system, not an exotic “facts about a place” list. Explain adaptation without implying that environment mechanically determines culture.",
