      "line_start": 211,
      "line_end": 226,
      "kind": "curriculum_or_design_reference",
      "body": "**Core question:** How are resources and economic activities distributed, managed and connected, and what trade-offs follow?\n\nCore modules:\n- Resource planning, land use, soils, soil erosion and conservation.\n- Forest and wildlife conservation; biodiversity and human pressure.\n- Water scarcity, multipurpose projects, watershed management and competing uses.\n- Agriculture, crop patterns, irrigation, institutional/technological factors and sustainability.\n- Minerals and energy resources, distribution, extraction and conservation.\n- Manufacturing industries, location factors, industrial regions, pollution control.\n- Transport, communication and trade as economic lifelines.\n- Developmental trade-offs: livelihoods, infrastructure, regional inequality, environmental costs and sustainability.\n\nTeacher emphasis: distinguish location factors from location outcomes; distinguish national aggregate gains from distributional consequences; analyse infrastructure as a network rather than a memorised list.",
