      "body": "**Core question:** What mechanisms create and transform the physical Earth system?\n\nMajor areas:\n- Geography as a discipline; physical/human geography and systematic/regional approaches.\n- Earth’s origin and evolution; geological time and evidence.\n- Interior of Earth, seismic waves, rocks and minerals, plate tectonics, earthquakes and volcanoes.\n- Geomorphic processes: endogenic/exogenic forces, weathering, mass wasting, erosion, transportation and deposition; landform development.\n- Atmosphere: composition, structure, insolation, heat budget, temperature, pressure, circulation, humidity, clouds and precipitation.\n- Weather systems, air masses, fronts, cyclones and climate patterns.\n- Oceans: relief, temperature, salinity, waves, tides and currents.\n- Life on Earth: biosphere, ecosystems, biomes, soils and environmental relationships.\n- India’s physiography, drainage, climate, soils, vegetation and natural hazards.\n- Practical geography: maps, scales, projections, statistical handling and spatial data methods; exact module coverage must be checked against the available practical-work volume.\n\nTeacher emphasis: teach processes through energy, force, material movement, feedback and timescale. Do not turn plate tectonics or monsoon into a set of isolated definitions.",
