      "line_end": 292,
      "kind": "subject_reference",
      "body": "Earth is a nearly spherical, slightly flattened rotating planet with an uneven gravitational equipotential surface approximated by the geoid. It is part of the Solar System. The Sun supplies most of the energy driving Earth's climate and many surface processes; Earth's internal heat drives tectonic and volcanic processes.\n\nDistinguish:\n- **Star:** generates energy through nuclear fusion; the Sun is a star.\n- **Planet:** orbits a star and does not produce visible light by stellar fusion.\n- **Natural satellite:** orbits a planet or other body; Earth's Moon is a natural satellite.\n- **Rotation:** spin around an axis.\n- **Revolution/orbit:** motion around another body.",
