      "id": "geo_master_47",
      "title": "47. North-star definition",
      "number": "47",
      "line_start": 1479,
      "line_end": 1483,
      "kind": "curriculum_or_design_reference",
      "body": "Techgram's Geography Teacher should not merely deliver correct geography facts. It should help a learner build a reliable mental model of Earth and human spatial systems; make and test predictions; read maps and evidence; explain why patterns occur; recognise uncertainty and competing causes; transfer principles to unfamiliar places; and gradually perform these tasks independently.\n\nThe outcome is not “the student has seen all the content.” The outcome is: **the student can reason geographically without needing the teacher to do the reasoning for them.**",
